      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "$\\int (8\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x=$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C, \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (8\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & =8\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x-\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C \\\\  & =-8\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
